Q: How to add a script to a wordpress page based on category A: <p>You can load a <a href="https://dev-with-purpose.pantheonsite.io/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">script</a> only for a specific category by checking the category before enqueuing the script in your theme's <code>functions.php</code> file.</p>
<pre><code>function load_category_script() {
    if (is_category('news')) { // Replace 'news' with your category slug
        wp_enqueue_script(
            'custom-script',
            get_template_directory_uri() . '/js/custom.js',
            array(),
            '1.0',
            true
        );
    }
}
add_action('wp_enqueue_scripts', 'load_category_script');
</code></pre>
<p>If you want the script only on <strong>single posts</strong> in a category:</p>
<pre><code>function load_post_category_script() {
    if (is_single() &amp;&amp; has_category('news')) {
        wp_enqueue_script(
            'custom-script',
            get_template_directory_uri() . '/js/custom.js',
            array(),
            '1.0',
            true
        );
    }
}
add_action('wp_enqueue_scripts', 'load_post_category_script');
</code></pre>
<p>Replace <code>'news'</code> with your category slug and update the script path as needed.</p>

